On Friday, February 24, 2012 9:04:37 PM UTC+4, selpa'i wrote:
>
>  No, Loglan had cases, similar to BAI, but not quite the same. For example 
> you'd have a case tag that tagged "recipient" or "agent". So with dunda, 
> you could use the recipient tag to mark the recipient instead of having to 
> put it in dunda3. The difference is that these tags were much less specific 
